    "title": "pandas.DatetimeTZDtype.tz — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeTZDtype.tz#\n\n- property DatetimeTZDtype.tz[source]#\n- The timezone. Returns the `datetime.tzinfo` object associated with this\ndtype, representing the timezone used for localization.See also \n  - `DatetimeTZDtype.unit`\n  - Retrieves precision of the datetime data.\n Examples >>> from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo >>> dtype = pd.DatetimeTZDtype(tz=ZoneInfo(\"America/Los_Angeles\")) >>> dtype.tz zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(key='America/Los_Angeles')",
